{"id": "valpaca0032", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So I went to a place called the street food market, and it was just like a huge area with all these little stalls selling different kinds of Thai food. They had things like pad thai, which is stir- fried noodles with vegetables and sometimes chicken or shrimp. There were also cur ries, which are really tasty, made with coconut milk and lots of spices. And then there were some fruit stands where they sold fresh tropical fruits like mango es, bananas, and papayas. It was so much fun trying all the different dishes and tasting the unique flavors of T hailand's cuisine.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
