{"id": "valpaca0040", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Canada was colon ized in the late 1 5 th century by French and British explorers. The first permanent settlement s were established along the St. Lawrence River in the early 1600s, primarily by the French, though contact with Indigenous people had occurred long before that.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0044", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I think it's because we evolved to believe in God. And the reason is that if you have a group of people, let' s say a tribe of hunter-gather ers, and some of them believe in God and some don't, then the ones who believe in God are going to be more likely to cooperate with each other. They're going to share food when they find it. They're going to look out for each other. So they're going to be more successful as a group. And so over time, those genes that make you believe in God are going to spread through the population.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0048", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The moon is visible during the day because it reflects sunlight, just like any other object. When the sun is out, even if it's bright, the moon can still be seen as long as it's above the horizon. Sometimes it' s easier to spot during the day when there are fewer clouds or less light pollution. It' s not unusual at all!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0052", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Yeah, that sounds really good. So, yeah, Flæskest ig is basically just a Danish stewed pork dish. And it's kind of like a pot roast in some ways, but it's got some different ingredients and spices that are unique to Danish cuisine. So you would start with about one pound of pork shoulder or chuck, cut into bite-sized pieces. Then you'd se ar the meat in a large pot over medium heat until browned on all sides. After removing the meat from the pot, add a chopped onion and two car rots to the same pot and cook them for about five minutes until they soften slightly. Next, add four cups of beef broth, two bay leaves, half a teaspoon of ground all spice, and a pinch of salt and pepper. Bring this mixture to a boil, then reduce the heat to low and let it simmer uncovered for about an hour and a half. Once the liquid has reduced by half and the meat is tender, return the meat to the pot and continue cooking for another 20 minutes. That should be ready to serve. It'", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0056", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": null, "no_speak": true, "answer_text": "", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 0, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0060", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Walt Disney was born in 1901. He grew up in Marceline, Missouri, and he loved drawing cartoon s when he was a child. He started working for an animation studio called Laugh-O-Gra ph in Kansas City as a teenager. And then later on, he moved to Los Angeles, where he worked at another animation studio called the I n dependence Film Corporation. He eventually founded his own company, the Disney Brothers Studio, which became known as Disney Studios. And they made their first animated short film in 19 28, called Steamboat Willie. It featured the character Mickey Mouse, who became one of the most famous characters in history. Dis ne y went on to create many other successful films and TV shows, including Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs, Pinoc chio, Fant asia, and Bambi. He also helped to establish Disneyland in Anaheim, California, in 195 5, which has since become one of the world's most popular theme parks. Walt Disney passed away in 1 966, but his legacy continues to inspire people around the", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0064", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Yeah, I mean, that' s a great idea. You can find plenty of Israeli recipes online. One recipe for cheese burekas is to make a dough with flour, oil, and water, roll it out into thin layers, fill them with cheese, and bake until golden brown.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0068", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, well, the airplane was invented by the Wright brothers. And they were two guys who lived in Ohio. They built their first plane in a bicycle shop. And then they took it to Kitty Hawk, North Carolina, and flew it there for the first time.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0072", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Sure, I can help you with that. If your nephew is into action and adventure, the new Mario K itti Party game just came out recently, so that might be a fun choice. It's full of mini games and lots of color ful characters he'll probably enjoy. Or if he likes something a bit more intense, there's also the new Luigi' s Mansion 3, which has really cool ghost- hunting gameplay. And for fans of racing or strategy, Super Smash Bros. Ultimate actually just got an update with even more character s now, so that could be a great option too. Do you know what kind of games he usually plays? That might help narrow it down further.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 33, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "valpaca0076", "pool": "valpaca", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I'd be happy to help. Vi daltono is a traditional Uruguayan dish that's often served during asado s or family gathering s. It's basically a large, round, stuffed meat pie made with beef and pork mixed with vegetables like onion s, peppers, and garlic, all wrapped in a dough crust. To make it, you'll need ground beef and pork, chopped onions, green pepper s, garlic, salt, and pepper for seasoning, plus some flour to bind the filling together. For the dough, use flour, water, and a little bit of oil. Start by sa uteing the chopped vegetables in a pan until they' re soft, then mix them into the ground meat along with seasonings and enough flour to hold the mixture together without being too dry. Knead the dough until it forms a smooth ball, let it rest briefly, then roll it out thin enough to cover your chosen container— traditionally an earthenware bowl or mold. Fill the mold with the meat mixture, seal the edges if needed, and bake it slowly at a low temperature until the crust is golden brown and cooked through. This can take several hours, but the result is worth the wait. It’s hearty, flavorful, and perfect for sharing with friends and family. Give it a try, and enjoy your Uruguayan culinary adventure!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 54, "carrier_ended": null}
